Description: Leave a window the user closes out of the session, the last one too.
 Text Editor removes a window the user closes from its session, with its documents, except the last one: closing the
 last window saves the session with that window, which the next start restores, so after closing every window one
 by one the last of them returns. The window the user closes last now leaves the session as well, before the save
 Text Editor quits after, and the next start opens a new window instead. A document with unsaved changes is still
 offered for saving or discarding before its window closes.
 .
 Every window still returns when Text Editor ends without the user closing its windows: the quit action, Ctrl+Q,
 saves the session with every window before quitting, so does the end of the desktop session, and the session
 autosaved last stays when Text Editor ends on SIGTERM or in a crash. A window destroyed without the user closing it
 stays in the session as before.
Author: Mitar
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-11
